# Skill router

**One owner per turn.** Do not half-run two skills. Explicit `/slash` wins over inference.

## Priority (first match wins)

1. Pack meta / tighten skills → `/upgrades`
2. Commit / push / publish → `/ship` (after implement/fix done)
3. Verdict only / pre-merge check → `/review`
4. Durable project problem / knowledge note → `/note`
5. UI demo · HTML clone · static HTML · multi-todo `.plan.md` graph → `/plan`
6. Product feature needing **≥2 slices** or an explicit **gated pipeline** (migrate + review + ship as slices) → `/feature`
7. Unknown-cause bug / flaky / unknown-cause wrong data → `/fix`
8. Clear **single** capability → `/make`

## Signal table

| Signal in the message | Prefer | Not |
|----------------------|--------|-----|
| Unknown-cause bug / flaky / unknown-cause wrong data / “broke” | `/fix` | `/make` |
| Known cause + clear patch | `/make` | `/fix` |
| Clear new capability / “add X” (one patch shape, even MED/HIGH) | `/make` | `/fix`, `/feature` |
| Single-capability schema/migration (one patch shape) | `/make` (`--full` / auto-full) | multi-slice `/feature` for that alone |
| UI demo / HTML clone / static HTML / multi-todo screen build | `/plan` | `/feature`, `/fix`, product screen in the app |
| Product feature ≥2 slices / migrate+review+ship as slices | `/feature` | `/plan`, one-patch `/make` |
| Want verdict only / pre-merge check | `/review` | `/make`, `/fix` |
| Commit / push / publish | `/ship` | implementing in same breath |
| Remember problem+fix / project knowledge note | `/note` | `/plan` for task graphs |
| Improve this pack’s skills | `/upgrades` | app `/make` |

## Anti-overlap

| Temptation | Do instead |
|------------|------------|
| `/feature` for one `/make`-sized change | `/make` |
| `/feature` because the change is MED/HIGH (one patch) | `/make` then `/review` then `/ship` |
| `/feature` for one migration-sized change | `/make --full` (+ enterprise-safety) |
| `/plan` for gated product + migrate + review | `/feature` |
| `/plan` for a product screen in the app | `/make` (or `/feature` if ≥2 slices) |
| `/fix` a greenfield UI clone | `/plan` |
| `/make` when cause unknown | `/fix` |
| `/note` a full multi-step build plan | `/plan` |
| Dump every chat prompt via `/note` | daily hooks → `.cursor/notes/daily/` |

## Same-message combos

- Code + “ก็ commit ด้วย” → finish `/make` or `/fix` first; then **MED/HIGH app** → `/review` then `/ship` (or explicit waive); pack-only LOW wording → `/ship` OK; pack always-on / REPORT / slash-rename → `/review` then `/ship`.
- Same message names both `/review` and `/ship` → run **`/review` first** (do not let `/ship` priority skip the verdict). After verdict clear, `/ship` needs its own confirm.
- Natural-language “review and commit/ship” (no slashes) → same order: verdict first, then `/ship` with confirm.
- “Build UI and fix the bug” → cause unclear → `/fix` first; else `/plan` with `/make`+`/fix` todos.
- Slash named explicitly → that skill wins (except review+ship combo above).
